//! Display-only star field: naked-eye stars, constellation figures and boundaries.
//!
//! OWNER: star-field agent. CONVENTIONS 13.6: nothing here is ever a direction source
//! for sight reduction, the solver, the planner's navigation candidates or an accuracy
//! claim. No crate on the navigation path may depend on this one; only the adapters,
//! `skyfix-wasm` and `skyfix-cli` (`skyfix sky`), join it with the engine to label
//! constellations (a test in `tests/crate_boundary.rs` holds the line).
//!
//! What is embedded (all of it under `data/`, generated by `tools/starfield/build.py`;
//! provenance in `docs/THIRD_PARTY.md`, section "Star field and constellations"):
//!
//! | data | source | licence |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | 9 095 stars (`stars.bin`) | Yale Bright Star Catalogue, 5th revised ed., as NASA HEASARC's `bsc5p` table | U.S. Government Work |
//! | 252 star names (`names.txt`) | names in common use (IAU WGSN), Nautical Almanac spelling for the 58 navigational stars | facts |
//! | 88 stick figures (`figures.txt`) | drawn by this project | MIT OR Apache-2.0 |
//! | IAU boundaries (`boundaries.txt`) | Delporte (1930), B1875.0 corners | facts, public domain |
//!
//! Modules:
//!
//! - [`catalog`]: the stars, their designations and names;
//! - [`apparent`]: apparent places of date for every star at once, through exactly the
//!   chain `skyfix_ephemeris::frames` uses for the navigational stars;
//! - [`constellations`]: figures, label positions, `constellation_at` and the boundary
//!   polylines for drawing;
//! - [`navigational`]: which catalogue entry each of the 58 navigational stars is.
//!
//! Accuracy (measured, `docs/ACCURACY.md`, "Star field"): apparent places agree with
//! Skyfield to well inside the 0.1' target of CONVENTIONS 13.7, and `constellation_at`
//! agrees with Skyfield's constellation map everywhere except, possibly, within an
//! arcsecond of a boundary.

pub mod apparent;
pub mod catalog;
pub mod constellations;
pub mod navigational;
